{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794568123006,"sessionID":"ses_e2b67d7f8ffeFiRgovIWES9WLX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-0da7f280-e4ea-4895-9b59-b10d6d6975ba","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"oldString":"else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")","newString":"else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n        if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n            if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n            for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n                if not isinstance(x, str):\n                    raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n                try:\n                    base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")","filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -148,15 +148,25 @@\n     if body.get(\"outcome\") not in OUTCOMES:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: outcome must be one of {OUTCOMES}\")\n     _check_digests(_need(body, \"evidence\", list, where), f\"{where}.evidence\")\n else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n-    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n+    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n     if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n     try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n         base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n     except ValueError:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n+    if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n+        if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n+            raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n+        for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n+            if not isinstance(x, str):\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n+            try:\n+                base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")\n extra = set(body) - allowed\n if extra:\n     raise Bad(f\"{where}: unknown body fields {sorted(extra)}\")\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -148,15 +148,25 @@\n     if body.get(\"outcome\") not in OUTCOMES:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: outcome must be one of {OUTCOMES}\")\n     _check_digests(_need(body, \"evidence\", list, where), f\"{where}.evidence\")\n else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n-    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n+    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n     if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n     try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n         base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n     except ValueError:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n+    if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n+        if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n+            raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n+        for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n+            if not isinstance(x, str):\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n+            try:\n+                base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")\n extra = set(body) - allowed\n if extra:\n     raise Bad(f\"{where}: unknown body fields {sorted(extra)}\")\n \n","additions":11,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794568122993,"end":1794568123004}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the task. I need to:\n\n1. Add a function `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` to `record/record.py`\n2. Wire it into wherever orphans are checked (in `cmd_monitor`)\n3. Ensure all existing tests pass\n\nLet me analyze the requirements for `_orphan_entries_problem`:\n- `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]` is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes\n- Return `None` when the decoded entries are exactly the attested range:\n  - Count must be `to_seq - from_seq + 1`\n  - First entry's `prev` must match `pred[\"prev_sha256\"]`\n  - Each next entry chains from previous one's sha256\n  - Last entry's sha256 must equal `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`\n- Otherwise return a short problem string:\n  - Contains \"range\" when count is wrong\n  - Contains \"chain\" when an entry's `prev` doesn't link\n  - Contains \"head\" when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`\n\nLooking at the `cmd_monitor` function, I can see where orphans are processed (around line 525-536). The orphan's statement is parsed and the predicate is extracted. I need to add the check for `entries_b64` there.\n\nLet me first check if orphans currently have `entries_b64` in their body schema. Looking at line 152, the allowed fields for orphan are `{\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}`. So I need to add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields.\n\nLet me implement this step by step:\n\n1. Add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan kind\n2. Implement `_orphan_entries_problem` function\n3. Wire it into `cmd_monitor` where orphans are checked\n\nLet me start by implementing the function.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d498726b001izHYqk2d9HW53N","sessionID":"ses_e2b67d7f8ffeFiRgovIWES9WLX","messageID":"msg_1d49835dc001f7bV9yl1i1Nk92"}}
