{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794568156258,"sessionID":"ses_e2b67d7f8ffeFiRgovIWES9WLX","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-0f84536e-43d8-4b1b-b45f-3cca9a25232f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport record as R\nimport base64, hashlib, json\n\n# Create a simple chain\nchain = []\nfor i in range(3):\n    e = {'seq': i+1, 'prev': chain[-1][1] if chain else None, 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'c{i}', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'd'}}\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    h = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n    chain.append((e, h))\n\n# Create a predicate for entries 1-2\npred = R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2)\nprint('pred:', pred)\n\n# Create entries_b64 for entries 1-2\nentries_b64 = [base64.b64encode(R.canonical(chain[0][0])).decode(), base64.b64encode(R.canonical(chain[1][0])).decode()]\n\n# Test valid orphan\norphan = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64}}\nprint('Valid:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan, pred))\n\n# Test wrong count\norphan2 = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64[:1]}}\nprint('Wrong count:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan2, pred))\n\n# Test broken chain - modify prev of second entry\ne2_bad = dict(chain[1][0])\ne2_bad['prev'] = '0'*64\nentries_b64_bad = [entries_b64[0], base64.b64encode(R.canonical(e2_bad)).decode()]\norphan3 = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64_bad}}\nprint('Broken chain:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan3, pred))\n\n# Test wrong head - modify last entry\ne2_bad2 = dict(chain[1][0])\ne2_bad2['body']['claim'] = 'changed'\nentries_b64_bad2 = [entries_b64[0], base64.b64encode(R.canonical(e2_bad2)).decode()]\norphan4 = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64_bad2}}\nprint('Wrong head:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan4, pred))\n\n# Test missing entries_b64\norphan5 = {'body': {}}\nprint('Missing:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan5, pred))\n\""},"output":"pred: {'from_seq': 1, 'to_seq': 2, 'prev_sha256': None, 'head_sha256': 'fea35094c7243a851ef6372b9a9d2b4da9a74d0ccb80c3c9a5c6890a5a3b54af'}\nValid: None\nWrong count: range count 1 != 2\nBroken chain: chain broken at entry 1\nWrong head: head mismatch 083559e700e6954515c00016c1bf763100c13b507a485de91ba6fb5718a0fefc != fea35094c7243a851ef6372b9a9d2b4da9a74d0ccb80c3c9a5c6890a5a3b54af\nMissing: missing entries_b64\n","metadata":{"output":"pred: {'from_seq': 1, 'to_seq': 2, 'prev_sha256': None, 'head_sha256': 'fea35094c7243a851ef6372b9a9d2b4da9a74d0ccb80c3c9a5c6890a5a3b54af'}\nValid: None\nWrong count: range count 1 != 2\nBroken chain: chain broken at entry 1\nWrong head: head mismatch 083559e700e6954515c00016c1bf763100c13b507a485de91ba6fb5718a0fefc != fea35094c7243a851ef6372b9a9d2b4da9a74d0ccb80c3c9a5c6890a5a3b54af\nMissing: missing entries_b64\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport record as R\nimport base64, hashlib, json\n\n# Create a simple chain\nchain = []\nfor i in range(3):\n    e = {'seq': i+1, 'prev': chain[-1][1] if chain else None, 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'c{i}', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'd'}}\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    h = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n    chain.append((e, h))\n\n# Create a predicate for entries 1-2\npred = R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2)\nprint('pred:', pred)\n\n# Create entries_b64 for entries 1-2\nentries_b64 = [base64.b64encode(R.canonical(chain[0][0])).decode(), base64.b64encode(R.canonical(chain[1][0])).decode()]\n\n# Test valid orphan\norphan = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64}}\nprint('Valid:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan, pred))\n\n# Test wrong count\norphan2 = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64[:1]}}\nprint('Wrong count:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan2, pred))\n\n# Test broken chain - modify prev of second entry\ne2_bad = dict(chain[1][0])\ne2_bad['prev'] = '0'*64\nentries_b64_bad = [entries_b64[0], base64.b64encode(R.canonical(e2_bad)).decode()]\norphan3 = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64_bad}}\nprint('Broken chain:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan3, pred))\n\n# Test wrong head - modify last entry\ne2_bad2 = dict(chain[1][0])\ne2_bad2['body']['claim'] = 'changed'\nentries_b64_bad2 = [entries_b64[0], base64.b64encode(R.canonical(e2_bad2)).decode()]\norphan4 = {'body': {'entries_b64': entries_b64_bad2}}\nprint('Wrong head:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan4, pred))\n\n# Test missing entries_b64\norphan5 = {'body': {}}\nprint('Missing:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan5, pred))\n\"","time":{"start":1794568156191,"end":1794568156248}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All existing tests pass. Now let me verify the implementation is correct by looking at the test for orphans. The existing test `test_orphan_entries_explain_attestations` creates an orphan without `entries_b64` and it still passes. This is because my validation in `cmd_monitor` only runs when there's a matching Rekor entry, not during ingestion.\n\nLet me also check if there's an issue with the `test_orphan_entries_explain_attestations` test - it creates an orphan without `entries_b64`, and my validation in `check_body` now allows `entries_b64` but doesn't require it. This is correct because the validation of `entries_b64` happens in `cmd_monitor` when checking against Rekor.\n\nLet me also verify the logic of `_orphan_entries_problem` more carefully:\n\n1. It checks that `entries_b64` exists (returns \"missing entries_b64\" if not)\n2. It checks the count matches `to_seq - from_seq + 1` (returns \"range count ...\" if not)\n3. It decodes each entry and checks it's canonical\n4. It checks the chain (prev matches) - returns \"chain broken at entry X\"\n5. It checks the head hash matches - returns \"head mismatch ...\"\n\nThis looks correct. Let me also run a quick test to make sure the function behaves correctly in isolation.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d498f41a001TzkghvGGj2ORmE","sessionID":"ses_e2b67d7f8ffeFiRgovIWES9WLX","messageID":"msg_1d498c4ad001AAa05MFjwsK0OQ"}}
