{"type":"text","timestamp":1794568163290,"sessionID":"ses_e2b67d7f8ffeFiRgovIWES9WLX","part":{"id":"prt_1d499085d001idvOeW75JAKXYo","messageID":"msg_1d4990166001abJjoTB9AlL9Va","sessionID":"ses_e2b67d7f8ffeFiRgovIWES9WLX","type":"text","text":"All 19 tests pass (1 skipped due to missing optional dependency). \n\n**Summary of changes to `record/record.py`:**\n\n1. **Added `entries_b64` to allowed orphan fields** (line ~152): Added validation that if present, it must be a list of valid base64 strings.\n\n2. **Implemented `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan, pred)`** (lines ~295-320): Validates that the orphan's `entries_b64` exactly matches the attested range:\n   - Returns `None` if valid\n   - Returns string with `\"range\"` if count is wrong (`to_seq - from_seq + 1`)\n   - Returns string with `\"chain\"` if an entry's `prev` doesn't link\n   - Returns string with `\"head\"` if the last entry's hash doesn't match `head_sha256`\n\n3. **Wired into `cmd_monitor`** (line ~569): After parsing the predicate from the orphan's statement, calls `_orphan_entries_problem` and reports any problem as a \"BAD\" finding.","time":{"start":1794568161373,"end":1794568163279}}}
